// idiom: secret
// summary: a name bound to one capability; its value reaches only the extern bodies that serve it
// rule: item 256: `secret NAME for CAP` binds NAME to CAP; the value is never in source, it is supplied at plug and is a local of the host body of every `extern emission[CAP]`
// rule: the value never leaves those bodies (a return, a crossing or an interpolation that carries it is refused), and a secret no emission extern serves is refused
// fill: secret api_key for net.send

secret api_key for net.send

extern emission[net.send] fn post(m: Str) -> Int = @py { return len(m) + len(api_key) }
